C DB id 55: INTEGER(CHARACTER) must validate the WHOLE substring as a
C standard input format (optional sign, digits, ONLY TRAILING blanks) --
C not parse a leading numeric prefix and silently ignore the rest the
C way strtod() does. M/S continuation-card pair below spliced verbatim
C from the real corpus repro (159-AGE.hal) to guarantee exact fixed-
C column alignment for the `C(7 TO 10)` to-partition subscript.
 T:
 PROGRAM;
    DECLARE C CHARACTER(10);
    DECLARE X INTEGER;
M    READALL(5) C;

M    X = INTEGER(C       );
S                 7 TO 10

    WRITE(6) X;
 CLOSE T;
